---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About — Disciple's Creed"
	description="The story behind the name, the logo, and the person leading the Disciple's Creed ministry."
>
	<!-- FIRST: The Story of the Name & Logo -->
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
		<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-12 sm:flex-row sm:gap-16">
			<div class="flex-shrink-0">
				<img
					src="/images/logo-full.jpg"
					alt="Disciple's Creed logo — winged sword and antique globe map"
					class="mx-auto w-48 rounded-2xl shadow-[0_16px_48px_rgba(0,0,0,0.6)] sm:w-56"
				/>
			</div>
			<div>
				<p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-gold">The Story</p>
				<h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-medium text-parchment sm:text-4xl">
					The Story of the Name & Logo
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
					In June 2023, I witnessed over 600 men and women at Lackland Air Force Base thunderously
					recite the Airmen's Creed. Among them was my grandson. After the ceremony, I exclaimed,
					<em class="text-parchment not-italic">"That's biblical."</em> A few days later, I composed
					the Disciple's Creed, which I believed encapsulated the biblical essence of every disciple,
					believer, of Jesus Christ, and the resolve every follower of Christ should embody.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
					P.S. Three years later, my grandson became a Pararescue Specialist. Their motto is even
					more biblical: <em class="text-parchment not-italic">"These Things We Do, That Others May Live."</em>
				</p>
				<p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
					The motto — <em class="text-parchment not-italic">No Reserve · No Retreat · No Regret</em>
					— belongs to William Whiting Borden (1887–1913), a Yale graduate who left wealth and
					comfort to carry the gospel to China. He died in Egypt at 25, before he ever arrived.
					Every disciple stands in that tradition.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Our Story -->
	<section class="reveal border-t border-gold-deep/20 bg-surface/40 px-6 py-20">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
			<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-parchment sm:text-3xl">Our Story</h2>
			<p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-xl text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
				The Disciple's Creed ministry exists to call the church back to her roots of biblical
				disciple-making as the God-ordained means by which Christ accomplishes His mission, in His
				church, the local community, and to the ends of the earth. Its central conviction is that
				Jesus did not merely command His followers to "make disciples," but to "make disciples of all
				nations," shifting disciple-making from a Western, provincial context to the global context
				of the biblical story.
			</p>
			<p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
				The ministry challenges the flawed theology that one can be a Christian without being a
				biblical disciple. It contends that faith and obedience are inseparable, salvation and
				lordship are interconnected, and being a believer is synonymous with being a Christ-defined
				disciple — one who counts the cost, takes up the cross, and lives for the Kingdom of God
				rather than personal comfort or cultural acceptance.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Meet the Founder -->
	<section class="reveal border-t border-gold-deep/20 px-6 py-20">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
			<div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-10 sm:flex-row sm:gap-14">
				<img
					src="/images/IMG_0267.jpeg"
					alt="Jeff Lewis with disciples"
					class="w-full rounded-2xl shadow-[0_16px_48px_rgba(0,0,0,0.6)] sm:w-72 sm:flex-shrink-0"
				/>
				<div>
					<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-parchment sm:text-3xl">Meet the Founder</h2>
					<p class="mt-1 text-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-gold">Jeff Lewis</p>
					<p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
						Jeff Lewis is the Founder and Director of Disciple's Creed. A discipler for 55 years —
						with the last 38 focused on how biblical disciple-making mobilizes the church — he has
						served as a university swimming coach, campus minister, church planter, pastor,
						denominational leader, and college professor at California Baptist University (1999–2019)
						and Oklahoma Baptist University (1996–1999). He has trained indigenous pastors, mission
						leaders, and missionaries in over 30 countries, planted and pastored two churches (Lock
						Haven, PA and Escondido, CA), and co-founded the Passion conferences (1997–2000). His
						published works include <em>God's Heart for the Nations</em>, <em>That All People's Might
						Sing His Praises: Calling: A Scriptural Journey</em>, and a contribution to
						<em>Discovering the Mission of God</em>.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
